  2249.9 ? dial=c15  "[p.85:] Enter any binary number from 0 through 15 on slide switches 3 through 6. Push pushbutton 6. The rotary switch will indicate the decimal equivalent of the binary number. [p.80:] (A slide switch RIGHT represents 0; a slide switch LEFT represents 1.) [BK1 p.20:] For example, when the pointer knob points at 1, the wiper arm makes an electrical connection between D1 and D16."
  8249.9 ? dial=c15  "[p.85:] The rotary switch is programmed so that when it turns to the energized terminal it will stop. Thus, setting a binary number in the slide switches will result in the same number being displayed on the rotary switch. / Enter any binary number from 0 through 15 on slide switches 3 through 6. Push pushbutton 6. The rotary switch will indicate the decimal equivalent of the binary number. [p.80:] (A slide switch RIGHT represents 0; a slide switch LEFT represents 1.) [BK1 p.20:] For example, when the pointer knob points at 1, the wiper arm makes an electrical connection between D1 and D16."
